# Restricted-identifier block list — one grep BRE pattern per line.
# Copy this file to .githooks/.blocked and replace the labels with real values.
# .blocked is gitignored and never pushed; these hooks reveal nothing on their own.
#
# Groups (opaque labels — fill in on your machine only):
#   BLOCKED_NAME_1        e.g. First Last
#   BLOCKED_NAME_2        e.g. an alias/handle
#   BLOCKED_EMAIL         e.g. you\.name@example\.com
#   BLOCKED_ORG           e.g. YourEmployer
#   BLOCKED_ORG_DOMAIN    e.g. employer\.com
#
# Notes:
#   - Escape regex metacharacters: '.' -> '\.'
#   - Matching is case-insensitive (grep -i).
#   - A bare org token (e.g. YourEmployer) already matches its domain substring.
#   - Patterns are grep ERE (the hooks and CI both match with `grep -iE`).
BLOCKED_NAME_1
BLOCKED_NAME_2
BLOCKED_EMAIL
BLOCKED_ORG
BLOCKED_ORG_DOMAIN

# Ready-to-use default (keep as-is, not a placeholder): Windows 8.3 short-path
# forms. The filesystem derives these from long names (e.g. a long user-profile
# dir becomes C:\Users\LONGNA~1), so a short path can leak an identity that the
# long-form patterns above never see. Anchored to \Users\ to avoid matching
# unrelated 8.3 names like PROGRA~1 (Program Files).
[Uu]sers\\[A-Za-z0-9]+~[0-9]
